<title>SINGAPORE: WBL full year net profit improves.</title>
<headline>WBL full year net profit improves.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   32.95	 vs	16.56</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)		2.00	 vs	 2.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	  29.00	 vs	14.60</p>
<p>    Turnover		    751.44	 vs     732.68</p>
<p>    Investment income	   0.23	 vs	(2.20)</p>
<p>    Interest expense	   22.54	 vs	23.14</p>
<p>    Depreciation		(29.22)	vs     (25.85)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     54.09	 vs	33.74</p>
<p>    Tax			    23.27	 vs	18.10</p>
<p>    Associates		    7.53	 vs	 7.08</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    (2.54)	vs	(0.27)</p>
<p>    Minorities		    1.45	 vs	 5.61</p>
<p>Dividend register/ pay</p>
<p>Note - WBL Corp Ltd said results improved due to better performance of the technology &amp; manufacturing, property &amp; leisure sectors. The extraordinary items comprised losses of S$15.1 million arsing from the discontinuation of certain activities and gains of S$13.3 million from the disposal of long term investments.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
